- \( v \) is the final velocity ( at the maximum height, \( v = 0 \text{ m/s} \))
- \( v_0 \) is the initial velocity (\( v_0 = 20 \, \text{m/s} \))
- \( a \) is the acceleration (acceleration due to gravity, \( a = -9.8 \, \text{m/s}^2 \))
- \( t \) is the time taken to reach the maximum height

