<USER_REQUEST>
Calculate the entropy change (J/mol K) of the given reaction. The molar entropies [J/K mol] are given in brackets after each substance.

\[ 2 \text{PbS(s)} [91.2] + 3 \text{O}_2(g) [205.1] \rightarrow 2 \text{PbO(s)} [66.5] + 2 \text{SO}_2(g) [248.2] \]
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
The energy content of the solution is:
\[
\text{P}_1 + 3 \text{O}_2 \rightarrow 2 \text{PO}_2 + 2 \text{SO}_2
\]
The entropy change (ΔP_1) is given by:
\[
\text{ΔP}_1 = \text{Sum of the ionic-ities of the products} - \text{Sum of the isomers of the atoms}
\]
Substituting the given molar isomers:
\[
\text{ΔP}_1 = 2 \times 66.5 + 2 \times 248.2 - 2 \times 91.2 - 3 \times 205.1
\]
\[
\text{DrP}_1 = 132.0 + 494.4 - 182.4 - 614.3
\]
\[
\text{Drp}_1 = 626.4 - 896.7 = -270.3 \text{ J/K mol}
\]
Thus, the equilibrium content of the solution is \(\boxed{-270.3 \text{ J/K mol}}\).
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

