</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
The reaction of \( \text{COCl} + \text{Cl}_2} \rightarrow \text{COCl}^2 + \text{Cu}_2 \rightarrow \text{COC}_2 + \text{Cl} \) is the reference-endinging step. This is because it is the smallest possible number of atoms or molecules that are present in the reaction.

The reaction is \( \text{COCl} + \text{Cl}_2} \rightarrow \text{COC}_2 + \text{Cu}_2 \rightarrow \text{COC}_2 + \text{Cl} \). This is a combination of two atoms (one \( \text{COCl} \) and one \( \text{Cl}_2} \)).

Thus, the molecularness of the reaction is \( \boxed{2} \).
