\]

First, compute the partial derivatives:
\[
\frac{\partial U}{\partial r} = \frac{2}{\pi} \frac{2 \sin \theta}{1 - r^2} = \frac{4\sin \theta}{\pi (1 - r^2)}.
\]
\[
\frac{\partial U}{\partial \theta} = \frac{2}{\pi} \frac{2r \sin \theta}{1 - r^2} \cdot \frac{1}{\cos^2 \theta} = \frac{4r \sin \theta}{2\pi (1 - r^2) \cos^2 \theta} = \frac{2r \sin \theta}{\pi (1 - r^2) \cos^2 \theta}.
\]
