**Proof:**  
1. Suppose \( \mu_n \) is a measure on \( \mathcal{F}_n \), and \( \mu \) is a measure on \( \mathcal{F} \).  
2. For any \( \mu \in \mathcal{F} \), define \( \mu_n \in \mathcal{F}_n \), where \( \mathcal{F}_n \in \mathcal{F} \).  
3. For any compact set \( C \), \( \mu_n(C) \leq \mu_n(\sigma \in \mathcal{F}_n : \sigma \subset C) \leq \mu(\sigma \in \mathcal{F} : \sigma \subset C) = \mu(C) \).  
