","To compute the natural frequencies and mode states of the biped-body system, we can use the following equation:

\[
\text{Ax} = \lambda \lambda^T \text{I} \text{x}
\]

where:
- \( A \) is the matrix of the system's system system
- \( \lambda \) is the eigenvector ( mode space)
- \( \lambda^T \) is the transpose of the eigenvector
- \( \lambda \) is the eigenvalues ( natural frequencies)
- \( I \) is the identity matrix

For \( N = 3 \) beads, the system can be represented as:

\[
\left[\begin{array}{c}m_t \lambda_1^2 \\ m_t \lambda_2^2 \\ m_t \lambda_3^2\end{array}\right] = \left[\begin{array}{c}k_t + K_c & -K_c & 0 \\ -K_c & k_t + K_c & -K_c \\ 0 & -K_c & k_t + K_c\end{array}\right] \left[\begin{array}{c}x_1 \\ x_2 \\ x_3\end{array}\right]
\]

**Step 1: Formulate the Eigen system**

The eigenvalues \( \lambda \) and eigenvectors \( \mathbf{x} \) are found by solving the characteristic equation:

\[
\det(\lambda^2 I - A) = 0
\]

