\[
\Delta \lambda = \frac{2h}{m_e c} = 0.0486 \, \text{Å}
\]
The percentage change is:
\[
\frac{\Delta \lambda}{\lambda} \times 100 = \frac{0.0486}{2.00} \times 100 = 2.43\%
\]
Thus, the maximum percentage change is \(\boxed{2.42\%}\).
