     \[
     \overline{h}_{\text{new}} = \overline{h} \left( \frac{\rho_{\text{new}}}{\rho} \right)^{0.5} \left( \frac{u_{\text{new}}}{u} \right)^{0.5} = 17.67 \times 5^{0.5} \times 2^{0.5} = 55.85 \, \text{W/m}^2\text{K}
     \]  
   - The new heat transfer rate \( Q_{\text{new}} \) is:  
     \[
     Q_{\text{new}} = 55.85 \times (0.2 \times 0.1) \times (100 - 50) = 55.85 \, \text{W}
     \]  
   - The percentage change is:  
     \[
     \text{Percentage Change} = 100 \times \left( \frac{55.85 - 17.67}{17.67} \right) = 316.2\%
     \]  

**Final Answers:**  
1. The initial rate of heat transfer is \(\boxed{17.67 \, \text{W}}\).  
2. The percentage change in heat transfer is \(\boxed{316.2\%}\).
