   The forces acting on the piston are:
   - Upward force due to pressure in cylinder A: \( P_A \times A_A \)
   - Downward forces:  
     - Weight of the piston: \( m_p \times g \)
     - Atmospheric pressure acting on the piston: \( P_0 \times (A_A - A_B) \)
     - Pressure in cylinder B acting on the piston: \( P_B \times A_B \)

